<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Essenes</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Essenes were a Jewish religious movement of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temple-in-jerusalem">Second Temple</a> period, active from about the 2nd century BCE to the 1st century CE. Described by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josephus">Josephus</a>, Philo and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pliny-the-elder">Pliny the Elder</a>, they lived communally, shared their property and practised strict ritual purity. Many scholars link them to the community at Qumran that produced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dead-sea">Dead Sea</a> Scrolls.</p></div>
